From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] WASM: let the UNO bridge generator see scaddins' interfaces

bugs/bug_addin_double_args.md: 11 analysis add-in functions return #VALUE! when a
formula carries no cached value. The report's signature table was right -- returns
`double` with more than one argument fails -- but its prose attributed that to
"double argument marshalling", which is not what happens.

The WASM UNO bridge does not dispatch generically. static/source/wasmbridgegen
emits one callVirtualFunction_<sig> thunk per signature it SEES, plus a dispatcher
that ends in

    throw RuntimeException("Wasm bridge cannot call virtual function with
                            signature " + signature)

and bridges/CustomTarget_gcc3_wasm.mk invoked it with only +udkapi +offapi.
com.sun.star.sheet.addin.XAnalysis lives in scaddins/idl, so the generator never
saw it and never emitted thunks for the signatures its methods need.

Measured, with the inner exception printed rather than the outer wrapper:

    getQuotient(double,double)  -> signature didd     MISSING
    getMround(double,double)    -> signature didd     MISSING
    getErf(XPropertySet&,...)   -> signature diidi    MISSING
    getSeriesSum(...)           -> signature didddi   MISSING
    ... and diiii, diiiii

The generated set contained only di, did, dii, diid, diii for double returns.

This also explains why SOME add-in functions worked: getWorkday and getDelta return
sal_Int32 and getDec2Bin returns OUString, and their signatures happen to coincide
with ones offapi already required. Coincidence, not design -- which is why the
failure looked like an arbitrary "double with 2+ arguments" rule. The decisive
control is getYearFrac vs getWorkday: identical argument sequences
[XInterface, long, long, void], differing only in return type, one fails and one
works.

Fix: pass scaddins' InternalUnoApi to the generator as a third registry, so the

AMENDED 2026-09-20 -- GATED ON ENABLE_WASM_STRIP_CALC. The original form of this
patch referenced scaddins UNCONDITIONALLY, and that broke every build on a
machine with an empty workdir -- which is every fresh CI runner, on every run.

scaddins is a CALC add-in. RepositoryModule_host.mk gates it behind
`$(if $(ENABLE_WASM_STRIP_CALC),, ... sc scaddins sccomp ... )`, so in a writer
or impress build the module is excluded, scaddins/InternalUnoApi_scaddins.mk's
`gb_InternalUnoApi_InternalUnoApi` registration never runs, and the order-only
`.dir` prerequisite that creates workdir/InternalUnoApi/ is never declared. make
then falls back to the bare pattern rule in solenv/gbuild/InternalUnoApi.mk
(`touch $@`, no directory) and the build dies with

    touch: cannot touch 'workdir/InternalUnoApi/scaddins.done': No such file or directory

4 of the 5 shipped modules are writer or impress (only `spreadsheets` is calc),
and `documents` is built FIRST -- so a cold build failed on module one, always.

WHY NOBODY SAW IT FOR A MONTH. engine/build/orchestrator.sh cleans only `instdir`
and `workdir/Rdb`, deliberately (1eb4c25d, 2026-01-31), and `git clean -fd` does
not remove `workdir` because it is gitignored. So on a developer machine
workdir/InternalUnoApi/scaddins.done persists from an earlier SPREADSHEETS build
-- where Calc is not stripped and scaddins really is built -- and the writer
build succeeds by touching a file another module left behind. The same failure
was hit on 2026-08-30 after a manual `rm -rf workdir` and is recorded in
bugs/BUG-28-pdf-import-parser-handoff-crash.md:1164, but it was attributed to the
deletion rather than to this patch, and the connection was never made.

The guard is the SAME EXPRESSION RepositoryModule_host.mk uses, deliberately: one
file said scaddins was conditional while this one said it was mandatory, and the
two must not be able to drift apart again.

This does not weaken the original fix. The defect it addresses
(bugs/bug_addin_double_args.md) is in Calc's analysis add-in functions, which do
not exist in a writer or impress build -- so where the guard suppresses the
dependency, there are no scaddins signatures to emit thunks for.
diff --git a/bridges/CustomTarget_gcc3_wasm.mk b/bridges/CustomTarget_gcc3_wasm.mk
index 15506e0d124b..004be554ab19 100644
--- a/bridges/CustomTarget_gcc3_wasm.mk
+++ b/bridges/CustomTarget_gcc3_wasm.mk
@@ -20,11 +20,13 @@ $(gb_CustomTarget_workdir)/bridges/gcc3_wasm/generated-cxx.cxx \
 $(gb_CustomTarget_workdir)/bridges/gcc3_wasm/exports: \
         $(call gb_Executable_get_target_for_build,wasmbridgegen) \
         $(call gb_UnoApi_get_target,udkapi) \
-        $(call gb_UnoApi_get_target,offapi)
+        $(call gb_UnoApi_get_target,offapi) \
+        $(if $(ENABLE_WASM_STRIP_CALC),,$(call gb_InternalUnoApi_get_target,scaddins))
 	$(call gb_Executable_get_command,wasmbridgegen) \
         $(gb_CustomTarget_workdir)/bridges/gcc3_wasm/generated-cxx.cxx \
         $(gb_CustomTarget_workdir)/bridges/gcc3_wasm/generated-asm.s \
         $(gb_CustomTarget_workdir)/bridges/gcc3_wasm/exports \
-        +$(call gb_UnoApi_get_target,udkapi) +$(call gb_UnoApi_get_target,offapi)
+        +$(call gb_UnoApi_get_target,udkapi) +$(call gb_UnoApi_get_target,offapi) \
+        $(if $(ENABLE_WASM_STRIP_CALC),,+$(call gb_UnoApiTarget_get_target,scaddins))
 
 # vim: set noet sw=4 ts=4:
